mothershipOS: streams and jacks configured by the launcher (mship.audio 1.0: one stream per phone audio device, so the
guest routes natively).
- MSHIP_SOUND_STREAMS: the streams' directions, e.g. `out,out,out,in,in,in` (default: one output, one input). Each
  stream is then a PCM device of its own in the guest (hda_fn_nid = stream id) and plays into / records from the
  ALSA PCM `mship_pcm<stream id>`.
- MSHIP_SOUND_JACKS: jacks as `<nid>:hp` / `<nid>:mic` (nid = the stream whose PCM the jack belongs to), reported
  as HDA pin configurations (headphone out / mic in, 1/8" jack, presence detect), so the guest's virtio-snd driver
  creates "Headphone" and "Mic" jacks with input switches (Android's wired accessory handling uses those).
- Jack events: the host writes `$HOME/jacks` (`hp=0|1 mic=0|1`); a watcher posts VIRTIO_SND_EVT_JACK_(DIS)CONNECTED
  into the event queue's buffers (kept from process_event, which used to ignore the queue) and updates the jack info.

